A||N||2||86SEFIERO||INSTALLING STEREO SYSTEM IN FIERO||||1||
Z||000000||86SEFIERO||06-03-2000||04:52 AM||||<BR>iF I INSTALL MY TWO AMPS IN THE REAR TRUNK WOULD THE TEMPERATURE FROM THE ENGINE COMPARTMENT BE TO HOT AND CAUSE AMPS TO OVRHEAT. i AM GOING TO INSTALL 10" SUBS BEHIND SEAT LIKE FIEROSOUND DID i WAS WONDERING IF AN 86SE REARFIREWALL HAS THE SAME STRUCTURAL ANGLE AS HIS OR DID THEY CONSTRUCK THE REAR FIREWALL DIFERRENTLY ON SOME MODELS?||||reg||1
Z||000001||86SE||06-03-2000||05:20 AM||||If the compartment gets as hot as mine it would.  Mine get over 150 mabey 250 on a really hot day after drivin hard.  Unless you have good air ventilation/circulation and some fans blowin on the amps you should be ok.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||06-03-2000||12:15 PM||||Putting amps in the rear truck you need to do 2 things. First add fans to keep the amps cooler or vent the trunk. Second, running the low level RCA lines past the engine will pick up alot of engine noise. You will need to shield them very well and use a good set of cables. Finally never run the low level lines into the inside of the car thru the ECM/engine harness area. It is easier and less noise to deal with if you mount the amps in the front under the spare tire.||||reg||1
